  {
   "title": "ESCALATION RISK — 5/5, held. Iran escalated in words from three institutions in three days and in deeds not at all; Oman is again the missing signature, for a second edition.",
   "text": "(i) THE KINETIC RECORD SINCE 5 SEPTEMBER IS EMPTY AND THE RHETORICAL ONE IS NOT. No CENTCOM release since 5 September on a direct read of its index; no acknowledged US strike on Iranian SOIL since 1 September, a seventh day; and no Iranian attack on any Gulf state since 3 September. (!) Bound both. The window is NOT kinetically quiet — US forces destroyed three Iranian tankers on 5 September, Iran claims three more, UKMTO logged disabling fire on the 6th and Jizan was struck on the 7th. And the tanker Downy was struck at the Kharg anchorage on 5 September, inside Iranian territorial waters, so the soil claim is a soil-versus-waters distinction rather than an absolute; no damage ashore was reported. (ii) Against that emptiness, three Iranian principals in three days: the parliament speaker on 6 September that the era of proportionate responses is over and that American oil and gas companies across these waters ‘share that exposure’; the security-council secretary on 7 September that the posture toward US warships and bases has been ‘fundamentally recalibrated’; the acting defence minister on 8 September, answering US claims that Iran cannot reach the blockading warships, ‘you will see the results’. All three are announcements. §9.11 governs: an announcement is not an event, and the channel is not moved on any of them — in either direction. (iii) Iran’s 5 September claim to have struck three tankers stays UNCORROBORATED into a fourth day; the newest UKMTO product is the one that logs the AMERICAN strikes. (!) The reported 4 September attack on US targets in JORDAN is STILL UNCONFIRMED on a second day, addressed by no government, and is never merged with the confirmed 31 August and 1 September Jordan events (§9.13). (iv) THE MEDIATOR IS THE MISSING SIGNATURE FOR A SECOND CONSECUTIVE EDITION, AND THE NEGATIVE IS NOW STRONGER, NOT WEAKER. Iran’s security-council secretary said on 6 September that Hormuz maps are agreed with Oman and will be signed within days; its foreign-ministry spokesman said on 7 September that the deal is in its final stages. (!) The method, stated in full: fm.gov.om homepage, Statements archive and on-site search for ‘Hormuz’, all read direct on 8 September. The site is CURRENT and not stale — its own footer reads last updated 7 September 2026 — and the three items it carries for that date are a Rwandan state visit and the Arab League. That distinction is the whole point of §9.23: a silence from a live publisher is evidence; a silence from a dead page is not. Neither confirmation nor denial exists. (v) And the counterparty that matters most has spoken against it: Washington has said it would not recognise an Iran–Oman agreement on the strait, and the State Department said on 8 September it will not allow Iran to ‘hold the global economy hostage’. An instrument announced by one party, unacknowledged by the second and pre-rejected by the third is not a mediated pause. The channel has been at 5/5 since 9 July and can register none of it (§9.7)."
  }
